# J37a — degraded taint: Health tones the cpg-graph row Warn (P2)  ⭐ release-blocking
#
# Keyless, deterministic. On a target with NO cpg graph, the deep auditor refuses
# to build implicitly and runs grep-only — so `health` must tone the cpg-graph row
# Warn with the `run cpg:build` remedy, and the pre-P2 sentence "graphs build
# implicitly on first hunt" must be gone. (J37b, the live grep-only run arm, needs
# a model key and is advisory — not encoded here.)
name: health tones the cpg-graph row Warn with the grep-only remedy
size: 120x40
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
# The degraded precondition: no whole-graph cpg artifact for this target.
shell: rm -rf @TMP_TARGET/.kuzushi/cpg-rs
shell: test ! -d @TMP_TARGET/.kuzushi/cpg-rs
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait: 6
submit: health
wait-for: 20 grep-only
snap: health-degraded
expect: cpg
expect: grep-only
expect: cpg:build
expect-not: graphs build implicitly on first hunt
ask: Is the cpg-graph row TONED Warn (check the .ansi), and is the remedy (`run cpg:build` / `taintTools=build`) actionable from the row itself? The pre-P2 "none prebuilt; graphs build implicitly" claim is now FALSE for the deep auditor and must be gone.
